      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T14:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With this sort of change it looks like `SkWriteBuffer` in general isn\u0027t useful without serial procs. With the defaults (for typeface and images) `SkWriteBuffer` generally \"just worked\" but without these defaults both serialization and deserialization no longer \"just work\" all the time so the user really needs to be forced to provide the procs. In other words, `SkWriteBuffer::setSerialProcs` should probably be removed and replaced with passing the procs into the constructor. Similar for `SkReadBuffer`.",
      "revId": "3b960adcc0b8ad33bccbeea6070a1ed03b85bc5c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23e46576_8e9e81f4",
        "filename": "src/text/gpu/Slug.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T20:16:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done for SkWriteBuffer. SkReadBuffer actually uses `SkImages::DeferredFromEncodedData` which makes use of registered codecs, so I think we can hold off on updating that for now. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "5168d480_491ed160",
      "revId": "3b960adcc0b8ad33bccbeea6070a1ed03b85bc5c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26b2de0a_ca6c1254",
        "filename": "src/text/gpu/Slug.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-13T20:30:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why should it be different? Couldn\u0027t we just say that `SkWriteBuffer` should use some registered (probably lossless) encoder by default. And maybe fail if one doesn\u0027t exist (I assume without looking that `SkReadBuffer` will fail to decode if there isn\u0027t a codec registered which will decode the data).",
      "parentUuid": "23e46576_8e9e81f4",
      "revId": "3b960adcc0b8ad33bccbeea6070a1ed03b85bc5c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3620d6f1_1f31c35b",
        "filename": "src/text/gpu/Slug.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-14T13:56:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In an ideal world, it probably should not be different. Since we\u0027ve decided the default behavior for WriteBuffer is to encode a null image if there is no default, the default for ReadBuffer should fail to decode and image if no proc was specified.\n\nIn a practical world, I don\u0027t want to make that change as it would probably involve a lot of churn with clients who use SKP serializiation.\n\nRegarding registered encoder - we don\u0027t have a way to register encoders, only decoders. I have no plans to add any.",
      "parentUuid": "26b2de0a_ca6c1254",
      "revId": "3b960adcc0b8ad33bccbeea6070a1ed03b85bc5c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
